  "headline": "Marginal-based DP synthesizer (d=16, 12 cells): naive PFN on synthetic rows is over-confident in 12, under-confident in 0 and calibrated in 0 cells (largest +0.186 at n=32, eps=1, k=4); quadrupling the synthetic rows changes its over-confidence by +0.003 to +0.040. The noise-aware PFN lowers NLL in 12/12 cells (gain +0.031 to +0.145 nats), with |over-confidence| <= 0.014 and accuracy within 0.016 of naive.",
  "h4_status": "partially-supported",
  "h4_note": "Label RR: a trained noise-aware PFN recovers 71-86% of the exact NLL gain over naive plug-in (E4-lite). Synthetic data: the sign of naive mis-calibration depends on the generator. It is under-confident for a noisy full histogram (D2-sparse, exact targets) and over-confident in 12/12 cells for a marginal-based, naive-Bayes-structured synthesizer (E4b-lite, trained networks: +0.081 to +0.186), where non-private naive Bayes is already over-confident (+0.098 to +0.165) and extra synthetic rows add little (+0.003 to +0.040). In E4b-lite the trained noise-aware PFN is calibrated (|over-confidence| <= 0.014) and lowers NLL in 12/12 cells. Open: richer-marginal generators (AIM/MST), real data, TabPFN scale."
